## Analytics Jobs

| Stage | Issue found | Rows | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|
| S2 Duplicates | Exact duplicate postings (every field equal except s_no) | 1,001 | Dropped (the only rows deleted in the whole pipeline) |
| S2 Duplicates | Near-duplicates after normalisation (same clean title, skills, city, experience and salary band; repost with another description) | 78 | Flagged is_near_duplicate; excluded from demand counts |
| S2 Duplicates | Possible reposts (same clean title, skills, city and experience, but a different salary band) | 2,777 | Flagged possible_repost only - kept in the sample (salary differs, may be a genuinely separate vacancy); used as a sensitivity check |
| S3 Text standardisation | job_desig: non-ASCII characters / leading-trailing / repeated spaces | 427 | Normalised |
| S3 Text standardisation | job_description: non-ASCII characters / leading-trailing / repeated spaces | 1,845 | Normalised |
| S3 Text standardisation | key_skills: non-ASCII characters / leading-trailing / repeated spaces | 20 | Normalised |
| S3 Text standardisation | job_description uses ';-' as bullet separators | 1,573 | Converted to sentences |
| S3 Text standardisation | Designations padded with recruiting noise ('Urgent Hiring', 'Walk-in', 'Opening for', '@Mumbai', bracketed notes) | 3,548 | Stripped into job_title_clean (original kept in job_desig) |
| S4 Parsing & types | Experience stored as text ('6-10 yrs') | 14,840 | Parsed to exp_min / exp_max / exp_mid / exp_range_width (years) |
| S4 Parsing & types | Salary only available as 6 text bands ('10to15') | 14,840 | Ordinal salary_band_ord 1-6, band low/high/mid (LPA), high_pay_15plus (target) |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Unparseable or inverted experience ranges | 0 | None found |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Lowest band (0-3 LPA) with 8+ years minimum experience - likely undisclosed salary coded as lowest band | 20 | Flagged salary_exp_inconsistent; excluded from salary models |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Very wide experience ranges (more than 8 years between min and max) | 237 | Kept; exp_mid used with care |
| S7 Harmonisation | job_type: one value spelt 5 ways (Analytics, analytics, ANALYTICS, analytic, Analytic) | 3,273 | Merged to 'analytics' |
| S7 Harmonisation | job_type missing for 76% of the original rows (12,011 of 15,841); 78% after removing exact duplicates - not usable as a classifier | 11,567 | Kept as job_type_tagged (0/1); analytics relevance re-derived from title + skills |
| S7 Harmonisation | location: 1,355 distinct strings, 16% list several cities, variants (Bangalore/Bengaluru, Gurgaon/Gurugram, Mumbai Suburbs, Sohna Road, Hyderabad/Secunderabad), states instead of cities, 'Anywhere Inindia' | 1,355 | Tokenised; 100+ variants mapped to canonical cities / metro areas; states and 'anywhere' -> Anywhere in India; derived primary_city, cities, n_cities, is_multi_city, city_tier |
| S7 Harmonisation | Overseas locations (Dubai, Canada, US, Singapore, Nigeria, Sweden, New Jersey ...) in an India dataset | 184 | Flagged is_international; excluded from the India market sample |
| S7 Harmonisation | key_skills free text: 8,462 distinct tokens after lower-casing | 14,840 | Lower-cased, trimmed, trailing '...' removed, synonym map (ML->machine learning, PowerBI->power bi, Base SAS->sas ...), de-duplicated per posting |
| S7 Harmonisation | Spelling/format variants of the same skill (power bi/powerbi, big data/bigdata, javascript/java script, c / c++ ...) | 122 | Auto-merged by letters-only key to the most frequent spelling |
| S7 Harmonisation | Junk skill tokens (empty, numbers like '1120', stray quotes, whole sentences > 45 chars, single letters) | 965 | Removed |
| S7 Harmonisation | Non-skill tokens mixed into skills: education (MBA, B.Com, B.Tech), job meta (fresher, BPO, non voice, present job), soft skills | 2,153 | Separated into education_mentioned, job_meta_tags, soft_skills; 'skills' keeps technical/domain skills only |
| S7 Harmonisation | key_skills truncated with '...' (87%) - lists are incomplete | 12,907 | Flagged; supplemented by skills found in the description (skills_from_desc) |
| S7 Harmonisation | 10,097 distinct free-text designations | 10,097 | Ordered keyword rules on job_title_clean (skills used when the title is uninformative) -> 18 role families + 'Other'; non-analytics guards (RCM, BPO, HR, SEO, IT) run before the generic 'analyst' rule; seniority (5 levels) |
| S8 Scope flags | Non-analytics roles inside 'Analytics Jobs' (software, BPO, HR, sales, finance, medical coding ...) | 9,673 | Flagged is_analytics_role=0; core analytics sample uses the 9 analytics families |
| S8 Scope flags | Low-quality 'data entry / work from home / part-time / freelance' postings | 166 | Flagged is_spam; excluded |
| S8 Scope flags | job_description missing (3,508 in the original file; count shown is after removing exact duplicates) | 3,371 | Not imputed (text); flagged desc_missing |
| S8 Scope flags | job_description truncated with '...' | 11,469 | Flagged desc_truncated; text treated as partial |
| S9 Derived variables | Skills recovered from job_description using a 488-skill vocabulary built from key_skills | 7,526 | skills_from_desc + union skills_all (descriptions also truncated, so a lower bound) |
| S9 Derived variables | No common key between the 4 files | 14,840 | Built a 5-dimension skill taxonomy (big data, maths-stats, coding, AI-ML, dashboards-storytelling) matching the JDS scores; each posting flagged dim_* - this is the bridge for linking market demand to the JDS success data |
| S10  | Manual audit of role_family on a final independent random sample of 150 postings | 150 | Exact family correct ~91%; analytics vs non-analytics split correct ~92%. Residual errors are ambiguous titles (e.g. 'SOC Analyst', 'Investment Analyst - Real Estate'); reported as a limitation |

## DataScience Jobs

| Stage | Issue found | Rows | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|
| S1 Structure & keys | reference_no is not unique: 134 numbers shared by 276 different rows | 276 | Kept original as reference_no; new surrogate key row_id (1..n) used as the record key |
| S3 Text standardisation | company_name leading/trailing/double spaces | 0 | Trimmed |
| S3 Text standardisation | Same employer group listed under two names (BNP Paribas / bnp paribas india solutions; HSBC / Hsbc Technology) - the units post the same titles with DIFFERENT salaries and openings, so they are separate listings | 13 | Kept as separate companies (not merged); linked through new company_group column |
| S3 Text standardisation | Placeholder / non-company employer names (Confidential, Xyz Company, Data Entry, Freelancer.com, Freelance Consultants) | 12 | Flagged is_placeholder_employer; excluded from company-level analysis |
| S4 Parsing & types | Salaries stored as text with an 'L' suffix ('7.8L') | 1,602 | Parsed to numeric lakhs per annum (LPA) |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Rule min <= avg <= max salary | 0 | 0 violations - internally consistent |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Minimum salary below 1 LPA (e.g. 0.2L = Rs 20,000 a year) - likely monthly/stipend figures entered as annual | 3 | Flagged min_salary_implausible; min salary not used in modelling for these rows (avg/max kept) |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Very wide salary range (max more than 6x min) | 34 | Flagged wide_salary_range; avg salary used as the main measure |
| S5 Validity & consistency | 'Senior' titles asking for 0 years minimum experience | 14 | Flagged senior_zero_exp (title/experience inconsistency) |
| S6 Outliers | num_of_jobs extremely right-skewed (median 22, max 4,200 = TCS Business Analyst); 3xIQR rule | 98 | Genuine bulk hiring - kept; flagged and log-transformed (log_num_jobs) for models |
| S6 Outliers | Average salary far from its job title's typical range (robust z > 3 within title, e.g. Flipkart Senior DS 82 LPA) | 11 | Kept (top employers pay more); flagged; salary_lpa_w = winsorised copy for models |
| S6 Outliers | min_experience above 12 years (max 21) | 12 | All are Data Architect rows - plausible; kept |

## JDS Skill Traits

| Stage | Issue found | Rows | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|
| S1 Structure & keys | Column name with a hyphen ('maths-stats_skills') - invalid in SAS/SQL | 1 | Renamed maths_stats_skills |
| S1 Structure & keys | id not unique: 2 ids shared by different people (different scores) | 4 | Kept as different people; surrogate row_id used as key |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Skill scores outside the documented 1-5 scale | 0 | None found |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Target salary_hike_high not 0/1 | 0 | None; class balance 53% high / 47% low (balanced) |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Missing values | 0 | None |
| S6 Outliers | Ceiling effect - share of perfect 5.0 scores: big_data 18%, maths_stats 41%, coding 45%, ai_and_ml 49%, dashboard_and_storytelling 58% | 293 | Kept (real scores); handled with rank tests, tree models and n_skills_at_max |
| S6 Outliers | Low outliers (|z| > 2.5) | 3 | Kept - genuine weak scores, scale is bounded |
| S9 Derived variables | Derived profile variables | 139 | skill_mean, skill_min, skill_range, n_skills_at_max, weakest/strongest skill, tech_core, communication_core, profile_type |

## SDS Personality Traits

| Stage | Issue found | Rows | Treatment |
|---|---|---|---|
| S1 Structure & keys | Column names with stray spaces (' extraversion', 'success_ classification_ high_low') | 2 | Trimmed; target renamed success_high |
| S1 Structure & keys | id not unique: 9 ids shared by different people | 18 | Kept; surrogate row_id used as key |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Trait scores outside a plausible 0-100 normalised range | 0 | None (observed 17-68) |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Missing values | 0 | None |
| S5 Validity & consistency | Target success_high balance | 161 | 53% high / 47% low (balanced) |
| S6 Outliers | Trait outliers (|z| > 2.5) | 4 | Kept - extreme but valid personality scores |
| S9 Derived variables | Derived variables | 161 | z-scores per trait, emotional_stability (reversed neuroticism), trait_mean (positive traits), dominant_trait |

## Validation checks (S10)

- [x] DS: row_id unique
- [x] DS: salaries numeric & positive
- [x] DS: min <= avg <= max
- [x] AN: s_no unique after de-dup
- [x] AN: no exact duplicates left
- [x] AN: experience parsed for all rows
- [x] AN: salary band parsed for all rows
- [x] AN: every row has a primary_city
- [x] AN: every row has a role_family
- [x] JDS: scores within 1-5
- [x] SDS: no missing values

